  <section class="sec" id="security">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Security and governance</p>
        <h2 data-split>Every AI call leaves a record. No report leaves unsigned.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="sec-grid">
        <div class="gov">
          <div data-reveal><svg class="i"><use href="#i-pen"/></svg><b>The AI never signs</b><p>Signing is a radiologist action. There is no setting that changes that.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><svg class="i"><use href="#i-spark"/></svg><b>AI text stays marked</b><p>Drafted text is labeled until a radiologist reviews or edits it.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><svg class="i"><use href="#i-doc"/></svg><b>Append-only audit log</b><p>Every AI call is recorded, including whether the request contained patient data.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><svg class="i"><use href="#i-stack"/></svg><b>Tenant isolation</b><p>Each institution's data, rulebooks and prompts stay inside its own tenant.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><svg class="i"><use href="#i-server"/></svg><b>On-prem or private cloud</b><p>Deploy inside your network, with a local model if you want nothing to leave it.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><svg class="i"><use href="#i-key"/></svg><b>SSO and MFA</b><p>Sign in through your identity provider over OIDC, with multi-factor authentication.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="console" data-reveal>
          <div class="console-h"><span>audit.log</span><span>append-only, illustrative</span></div>
          <ul class="log" id="log" aria-label="Illustrative audit log entries"></ul>
          <div class="console-f">Entries are written, never edited or deleted.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

